normalized.text:
{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the scgpt RNA encoder in a single-profile RNA-only setting, achieving validation accuracy of 0.4106 and F1 of 0.3785, lower than the pca_n2000 baseline (0.4849 accuracy, 0.4639 F1). The result suggests scgpt may underperform in single-profile settings compared to other encoders, but the exact contribution of the encoder versus profile setting remains uncertain. The lack of comparative experiments with other aggregation methods or fusion strategies limits conclusions about broader design implications."
}

